    "created_at": "2023-08-11T17:15:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-08-11T17:15:29Z",
    "body": "I'd also be interested in this feature. I'm currently using the [bobthefish](https://github.com/oh-my-fish/theme-bobthefish) theme/prompt and would really like to build a prompt like this in starship. bobthefish only distinguishes between \"no changes\" (green) \"dirty\" (unstaged changes, red) and \"staged\" (yellow). It does this by running `git diff --no-ext-diff --quiet --exit-code` (see https://github.com/oh-my-fish/theme-bobthefish/blob/master/functions/fish_prompt.fish#L1011-L1048 ) I don't know how expensive it is to run these commands in the branch module, but there is no output to parse, just an exit code that acts as a boolean. And you could check the config and only run the commands when the format requests the state\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
