    "updated_at": "2025-09-01T17:31:11Z",
    "body": "similar to [this comment](https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/3062#issuecomment-1280030329) I think adding the branch name to the git_status module would accomplish what all of us want and should be fairly easy.\n\ncurrently the status module calls `git status --porcelain=2` and importantly, it already adds the `--branch` flag which will give us the head an upstream branch names. All that would need to happen is to grab the name and make it available as a variable so we can disable the git_branch module and use the git_status module to add the branch name.\n\nWith that being said, there's an ominous comment and check before it will add the `--branch` flag:\n```rust\n        // for performance reasons, only pass flags if necessary...\n        let has_ahead_behind = !config.ahead.is_empty() || !config.behind.is_empty();\n        let has_up_to_date_diverged = !config.up_to_date.is_empty() || !config.diverged.is_empty();\n        if has_ahead_behind || has_up_to_date_diverged {\n            args.push(\"--branch\");\n        }\n```\nNot sure how much adding the `--branch` flag actually affects performance though.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
