    "created_at": "2026-05-20T11:32:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-20T11:36:56Z",
    "body": "Naive suggestion to expand style configuration:\n\n```toml\n[git_status]\nstyle = [\n  [\"$default\",                                   \"fg:color_fg0 bg:color_green\"],\n  [\"$untracked$staged$modified$renamed$changed\", \"bg:color_yellow\"],\n  [\"$conflicted\",                                \"bg:color_red\"],\n]\nformat = '([$ahead_behind $all_status ]($style))'\n```\n\n`style` would be a list of conditional matchers and an actual style. Matchers would be checked one-by-one, overriding previous possible matches. In order to have a default, a meta property `$default` would be created so it always matches.\n\nExample for configuration above, if there is a conflict:\n1. `$default` will match (always), so it sets `fg` to white and `bg` to green\n2. `$untracked$staged$modified$renamed$changed` won't match, so its style is skipped\n3. `$conflicted` will match, overriding `bg` to red",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
